{
  "version": "0.1",
  "status": "draft, hand-written; needs review by the medical team (source: TODO-cite)",
  "_notes": [
    "Purpose (docs/DECISIONS.md 19, 'No task, no data'): patient data only for a recognisable clinical TASK. engine/intent.py decides, after the clinical gate: once the role words are removed, the request must contain a recognised KB task, a named topic (rulebook/kb_overlay.json topics), an applicability item, or at least one clinical content word. Otherwise the screen is 'needs_task' with zero patient facts and a request to name the task.",
    "Clinical content words come from the KB itself (bundle tag words, slot labels, task_terms, topic terms, drug names in rulebook/drugs.json, the record's concept labels) plus the multilingual intent words below (clinical verbs and intent: assess, worry, before surgery, coming in, Aufnahme, abklären ...).",
    "Matching: accent-folded, lowercase, whole words; words of 6+ characters also match as a word prefix (German compounds, inflections). Phrases match as whole phrases.",
    "'never' words never count, even when a KB tag contains them: greetings, filler, test words. 'tag_stop' removes generic words from the KB tag vocabulary.",
    "Generic keywords only; no patient content.",
    "body_symptom_*: body parts and common symptoms (a symptom or body site names a clinical problem: 'GP, ingrown toenail', 'feeling thirsty')."
  ],
